  "body": "In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-style-element:update-a-style-block, the \"child text content change steps\" actually goes to the definition of [adopting steps](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt-ext) in the DOM spec rather than [child text content change steps](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-text-change-ext). In fact, this [looks](https://searchfox.org/whatwg-html/rev/404321b6535ae6f15a80708dc9e4038756ef5710/source#3155-3156) like an inadvertent copy-paste mistake:\r\n\r\n> ```html\r\n> <dfn data-x=\"concept-node-adopt-ext\" data-x-href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt-ext\">adopting steps</dfn>, and\r\n> <dfn data-x-href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt-ext\">child text content change steps</dfn> hooks</li>\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nFixing this would require first finding this code fragment (at the time of writing, the mistake is in line 3156), and then replacing the erroneous URL \"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt-ext\" with the correct URL \"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-text-change-ext\".",
